---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../components/ProjectCard.astro';
import { profile, projects, url } from '../data/site';
const nav = [['01', 'Selected work', 'projects'], ['02', 'Experience', 'experience'], ['03', 'A little about me', 'about'], ['04', 'Get in touch', 'contact']];
---
<Layout title="Austin Bwanika — Software Engineer & Data Science Student" description="Software engineering and data science with a practical focus. Explore Austin Bwanika’s projects, Metricell experience and work in machine learning.">
  <div class="portfolio-shell">
    <header class="intro">
      <a class="monogram" href={url()} aria-label="Austin Bwanika home">ab<span aria-hidden="true">.</span></a>
      <p class="eyebrow">Software engineering & data science</p>
      <h1>Austin <br />Bwanika<span class="terracotta">.</span></h1>
      <p class="intro-statement">Got a problem?<br /><em>I can fix it </em></p>
      <p class="intro-copy">Hi, I’m Austin. I build software and explore data to make everyday problems a little bit easier to solve.</p>
      <p class="current"><span aria-hidden="true" class="dot"></span>MSc Data Science · King’s College London</p>
      {profile.publicCv && <a class="text-link" href={url(profile.publicCv)}>Download CV</a>}
      <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="On this page">{nav.map(([n, label, id]) => <a href={`#${id}`}><span>{n}</span><span class="nav-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>{label}</a>)}</nav>
      <div class="social-links"><a href={profile.github}>GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={profile.linkedin}>LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>Email <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <p class="intro-foot">Built with care. Always learning.</p>
    </header>
    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
      <section id="projects" class="section work-section" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Selected work</p><span class="small-note">My greatest achievements</span></div>
        <h2 id="projects-title">A few things I’ve built<span class="terracotta">.</span></h2>
        <p class="section-lead">From reconciling payments to understanding football transfers. Different problems, the same curiosity.</p>
        <div class="projects">{projects.map((project, index) => <ProjectCard project={project} index={index} />)}</div>
        <div class="other-projects"><h3>Also on my workbench</h3>
          <article><h4><a href="https://github.com/AustinBwanika/music-converter">CrossTune <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h4><p>A Python tool for moving songs, albums and playlists between Spotify and Apple Music, with OAuth, pagination and rate-limit handling.</p><span class="mini-label">Python · Music APIs / 2024–2025</span></article>
          <article><h4>London Airbnb pricing</h4><p>A team project combining property and neighbourhood data. I developed and evaluated regression models; Random Forest reduced MAE from £44.61 to £36.74 against the linear baseline.</p><span class="mini-label">Python · pandas · scikit-learn / 2026</span></article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="experience" class="section" aria-labelledby="experience-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Experience</p><h2 id="experience-title">Building with a team.</h2>
        <div class="experience-heading"><div><h3>Placement Software Developer</h3><a class="company" href="https://www.metricell.com/">Metricell ↗</a></div><p class="date">Aug 2024 — Aug 2025<br />Horsham, UK</p></div>
        <p>A year working on telecommunications software, from network mapping to large-scale data processing.</p>
        <ul class="experience-list"><li>Technical lead for a team of three on an asset-management platform, defining the data architecture with stakeholders.</li><li>Built a CloudRF-powered mapping feature in TypeScript and C# to support radio-propagation analysis across more than 100 sites.</li><li>Wrote optimised queries for over 100 million image records and restored an archived database for a new initiative.</li><li>Owned a pilot computer-vision platform for road defects and documented the work to support future developers.</li></ul>
        <ul class="tags" aria-label="Technologies"><li>C# / .NET</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>React</li><li>SQL Server</li></ul>
      </section>
      <section id="about" class="section" aria-labelledby="about-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / A little about me</p><h2 id="about-title">Curiosity, in and out<br />of the code.</h2>
        <p>I’m a First-Class Computer Science graduate from the University of Surrey, now studying for an MSc in Data Science at King’s College London.</p>
        <p>I’m interested in the point where software engineering meets data: building something useful, understanding how it behaves, and finding ways to make it better.</p>
        <div class="education"><div><span class="mini-label">2026 — 2027 (expected)</span><strong>MSc Data Science</strong><span>King’s College London</span></div><div><span class="mini-label">2022 — 2026</span><strong>BSc Computer Science</strong><span>University of Surrey · First-Class Honours</span></div></div>
        <div class="outside"><span aria-hidden="true" class="asterisk">✳</span><div><h3>Outside the code</h3><p>Music is a big part of my life. I host The Kasetunes Show and enjoy sharing what I’m listening to. Away from the microphone, you’ll find me playing basketball — I’ve also captained my university’s recreational team.</p></div></div>
      </section>
      <section id="contact" class="section contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Get in touch</p><h2 id="contact-title">Something in mind?<br /><em>Let’s talk.</em></h2><p>For a role, a collaboration or a project you’re working on, I’d love to hear from you.</p><a class="contact-email" href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="social-links"><a href={profile.github}>GitHub ↗</a><a href={profile.linkedin}>LinkedIn ↗</a></div></section>
      <footer><span>© {new Date().getUTCFullYear()} Austin Bwanika</span><a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a></footer>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
